# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"
msgstr ""
"Ejemplo de simulador a pequeña escala {#small-scale-simulator-example}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This section uses a 10-site system to illustrate the AQC-Tensor workflow "
"step by step. We simulate the dynamics of a 10-site XXZ spin chain, a widely"
" studied model for examining spin interactions and magnetic properties.\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The Hamiltonian is as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Esta sección usa un sistema de 10 sitios para ilustrar el flujo de trabajo "
"de AQC-Tensor paso a paso. Simulamos la dinámica de una cadena de espín XXZ "
"de 10 sitios, un modelo ampliamente estudiado para examinar interacciones de"
" espín y propiedades magnéticas.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}_{XXZ} = \\sum_{i=1}^{L-1} J_{i,(i+1)}\\left(X_i X_{(i+1)}+Y_i Y_{(i+1)}+ 2\\cdot Z_i Z_{(i+1)} \\right) \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"El hamiltoniano es el siguiente:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}_{XXZ} = \\sum_{i=1}^{L-1} J_{i,(i+1)}\\left(X_i X_{(i+1)}+Y_i Y_{(i+1)}+ 2\\cdot Z_i Z_{(i+1)} \\right) \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $J_{i,(i+1)}$ is a random coefficient for edge $(i, i+1)$ and "
"$L=10$.\n"
msgstr ""
"donde $J_{i,(i+1)}$ es un coeficiente aleatorio para el enlace $(i, i+1)$ y "
"$L=10$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-"
"inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr ""
"Paso 1: Mapear las entradas clásicas a un problema cuántico {#step-1-map-"
"classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this step, we:\n"
"1. Define the Hamiltonian, observable, and initial state.\n"
"2. Compute the exact expectation value classically for later comparison.\n"
"3. Generate a high-accuracy Trotter circuit (the AQC target) and compress it into a low-depth ansatz using AQC-Tensor.\n"
msgstr ""
"En este paso:\n"
"1. Definimos el hamiltoniano, el observable y el estado inicial.\n"
"2. Calculamos el valor esperado exacto clásicamente para una comparación posterior.\n"
"3. Generamos un circuito Trotter de alta precisión (el objetivo AQC) y lo comprimimos en un ansatz de poca profundidad usando AQC-Tensor.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Set up the Hamiltonian, observable, and initial state {#set-up-the-"
"hamiltonian-observable-and-initial-state}"
msgstr ""
"Configurar el hamiltoniano, el observable y el estado inicial {#set-up-the-"
"hamiltonian-observable-and-initial-state}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/approximate-"
"quantum-compilation-for-time-evolution/extracted-outputs/527dbada-1.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/approximate-"
"quantum-compilation-for-time-evolution/extracted-outputs/527dbada-1.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compute the exact expectation value {#compute-the-exact-expectation-value}"
msgstr ""
"Calcular el valor esperado exacto {#compute-the-exact-expectation-value}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For a system of this size, we can compute the exact time-evolved expectation"
" value directly using matrix exponentiation. This serves as our ground truth"
" for evaluating the AQC circuit's accuracy.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para un sistema de este tamaño, podemos calcular el valor esperado "
"evolucionado temporalmente de manera exacta directamente mediante "
"exponenciación matricial. Esto sirve como nuestra referencia real para "
"evaluar la precisión del circuito AQC.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Generate the AQC target circuit {#generate-the-aqc-target-circuit}"
msgstr "Generar el circuito objetivo AQC {#generate-the-aqc-target-circuit}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We now construct the Trotter circuit that will serve as the AQC target. This"
" circuit uses many Trotter steps (32) for high accuracy. Because it will "
"only be simulated classically as an MPS&mdash;not executed on "
"hardware&mdash;the large depth is not a concern.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ahora construimos el circuito Trotter que servirá como objetivo AQC. Este "
"circuito usa muchos pasos de Trotter (32) para alta precisión. Dado que solo"
" se simulará clásicamente como un MPS&mdash;no se ejecutará en "
"hardware&mdash;la gran profundidad no es una preocupación.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Generate an ansatz, initial parameters, subsequent circuit, and a baseline "
"circuit {#generate-an-ansatz-initial-parameters-subsequent-circuit-and-a-"
"baseline-circuit}"
msgstr ""
"Generar un ansatz, parámetros iniciales, circuito posterior y un circuito de"
" referencia {#generate-an-ansatz-initial-parameters-subsequent-circuit-and-"
"a-baseline-circuit}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, we construct a \"good\" circuit with the same evolution time as the "
"AQC target but far fewer Trotter steps (only one). We pass this circuit to "
"`generate_ansatz_from_circuit`, which returns:\n"
msgstr ""
"A continuación, construimos un circuito \"bueno\" con el mismo tiempo de "
"evolución que el objetivo AQC pero con muchos menos pasos de Trotter (solo "
"uno). Pasamos este circuito a `generate_ansatz_from_circuit`, que "
"devuelve:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A general, parametrized **ansatz** circuit with the same two-qubit "
"connectivity.\n"
msgstr ""
"Un circuito **ansatz** general parametrizado con la misma conectividad de "
"dos qubits.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Initial parameters** that reproduce the input circuit when plugged into "
"the ansatz.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Parámetros iniciales** que reproducen el circuito de entrada cuando se "
"insertan en el ansatz.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We also construct:\n"
"- A **subsequent circuit** with one Trotter step that will be appended (uncompressed) after the AQC-optimized portion, following the approach in the [AQC-Tensor initial state tutorial](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-aqc-tensor/tutorials/01_initial_state_aqc.html).\n"
"- A **baseline Trotter circuit** using four Trotter steps over the full evolution time (`aqc_evolution_time + subsequent_evolution_time`). This serves as the comparison: it represents what you would run on hardware without AQC. The AQC ansatz (3 compressed steps + 1 uncompressed step) achieves better accuracy at lower depth.\n"
msgstr ""
"También construimos:\n"
"- Un **circuito posterior** con un paso de Trotter que se añadirá (sin comprimir) después de la porción optimizada por AQC, siguiendo el enfoque en el [tutorial de estado inicial de AQC-Tensor](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-aqc-tensor/tutorials/01_initial_state_aqc.html).\n"
"- Un **circuito Trotter de referencia** usando cuatro pasos de Trotter sobre el tiempo de evolución completo (`aqc_evolution_time + subsequent_evolution_time`). Esto sirve como comparación: representa lo que ejecutarías en hardware sin AQC. El ansatz AQC (3 pasos comprimidos + 1 paso sin comprimir) logra mejor precisión con menor profundidad.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/approximate-"
"quantum-compilation-for-time-evolution/extracted-outputs/78f2665e-1.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/approximate-"
"quantum-compilation-for-time-evolution/extracted-outputs/78f2665e-1.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Set up tensor network simulation and build the target MPS {#set-up-tensor-"
"network-simulation-and-build-the-target-mps}"
msgstr ""
"Configurar la simulación de redes de tensores y construir el MPS objetivo "
"{#set-up-tensor-network-simulation-and-build-the-target-mps}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We use the [quimb](https://github.com/jcmgray/quimb) matrix-product state "
"(MPS) circuit simulator, with JAX providing automatic differentiation for "
"the gradient-based optimization. We then build an MPS representation of the "
"target state and evaluate the starting fidelity between the initial ansatz "
"and the target. As the problem instance is a relatively small example, the "
"starting fidelity starts off quite high.\n"
msgstr ""
"Usamos el simulador de circuitos de estado de producto matricial (MPS) de "
"[quimb](https://github.com/jcmgray/quimb), con JAX proporcionando "
"diferenciación automática para la optimización basada en gradiente. Luego "
"construimos una representación MPS del estado objetivo y evaluamos la "
"fidelidad inicial entre el ansatz inicial y el objetivo. Dado que el "
"problema es un ejemplo relativamente pequeño, la fidelidad inicial comienza "
"siendo bastante alta.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Optimize the ansatz parameters {#optimize-the-ansatz-parameters}"
msgstr "Optimizar los parámetros del ansatz {#optimize-the-ansatz-parameters}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We minimize the `MaximizeStateFidelity` cost function using the L-BFGS-B "
"optimizer. The optimizer iteratively adjusts the ansatz parameters to "
"maximize the fidelity between the ansatz circuit and the target MPS.\n"
msgstr ""
"Minimizamos la función de costo `MaximizeStateFidelity` usando el "
"optimizador L-BFGS-B. El optimizador ajusta iterativamente los parámetros "
"del ansatz para maximizar la fidelidad entre el circuito ansatz y el MPS "
"objetivo.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Assemble the final AQC circuit {#assemble-the-final-aqc-circuit}"
msgstr "Ensamblar el circuito AQC final {#assemble-the-final-aqc-circuit}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With the optimized parameters in hand, we bind them to the ansatz and then "
"append the subsequent (uncompressed) Trotter step. The resulting circuit has"
" the depth of a single compressed Trotter step plus one uncompressed step, "
"but the compressed portion approximates the accuracy of 32 Trotter steps.\n"
msgstr ""
"Con los parámetros optimizados, los vinculamos al ansatz y luego añadimos el"
" paso de Trotter posterior (sin comprimir). El circuito resultante tiene la "
"profundidad de un único paso de Trotter comprimido más un paso sin "
"comprimir, pero la porción comprimida aproxima la precisión de 32 pasos de "
"Trotter.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/approximate-"
"quantum-compilation-for-time-evolution/extracted-outputs/e09e40de-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/approximate-"
"quantum-compilation-for-time-evolution/extracted-outputs/e09e40de-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-"
"problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr ""
"Paso 2: Optimizar el problema para la ejecución en hardware cuántico "
"{#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For this small-scale example, we use a fake backend (`FakeKyiv`) to simulate"
" hardware execution locally. We transpile both the AQC-optimized circuit "
"(`aqc_final_circuit`) and the baseline Trotter circuit (`baseline_circuit`, "
"four Trotter steps over the full evolution time, no AQC) to the backend's "
"instruction set architecture (ISA), with `optimization_level=3` to further "
"reduce circuit depth.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para este ejemplo a pequeña escala, usamos un backend falso (`FakeKyiv`) "
"para simular la ejecución de hardware localmente. Transpilamos tanto el "
"circuito optimizado por AQC (`aqc_final_circuit`) como el circuito Trotter "
"de referencia (`baseline_circuit`, cuatro pasos de Trotter sobre el tiempo "
"de evolución completo, sin AQC) a la arquitectura del conjunto de "
"instrucciones (ISA) del backend, con `optimization_level=3` para reducir aún"
" más la profundidad del circuito.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-"
"primitives}"
msgstr ""
"Paso 3: Ejecutar utilizando primitivas de Qiskit {#step-3-execute-using-"
"qiskit-primitives}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We use the [`EstimatorV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-"
"runtime/estimator-v2) primitive with the fake backend to run both the AQC-"
"optimized circuit and the baseline Trotter circuit, measuring the ZZ "
"observable for each.\n"
msgstr ""
"Usamos la primitiva [`EstimatorV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"ibm-runtime/estimator-v2) con el backend falso para ejecutar tanto el "
"circuito optimizado por AQC como el circuito Trotter de referencia, midiendo"
" el observable ZZ para cada uno.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format "
"{#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr ""
"Paso 4: Posprocesar y devolver el resultado en el formato clásico deseado "
"{#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We extract the expectation values from both runs and compare them to the "
"exact result. The baseline Trotter circuit shows what we would get without "
"AQC at the same circuit depth, while the AQC circuit demonstrates the "
"improvement from tensor-network optimization.\n"
msgstr ""
"Extraemos los valores esperados de ambas ejecuciones y los comparamos con el"
" resultado exacto. El circuito Trotter de referencia muestra lo que "
"obtendríamos sin AQC a la misma profundidad de circuito, mientras que el "
"circuito AQC demuestra la mejora gracias a la optimización mediante redes de"
" tensores.\n"

